00:39:03.450 --> 00:39:04.290
Me, too.

892
00:39:04.830 --> 00:39:11.870
You know, at 5 minutes 36 seconds, Dwight says, if you clench your buttocks together while walking, you can really take the pressure off your knees.

893
00:39:11.970 --> 00:39:13.070
Little tip there.

894
00:39:13.310 --> 00:39:14.410
Just a little tip.

895
00:39:14.690 --> 00:39:15.770
Well, I looked it up.

896
00:39:16.010 --> 00:39:16.850
Does it work?

897
00:39:16.950 --> 00:39:17.850
I was going to try it.

898
00:39:18.050 --> 00:39:23.130
Well, I read an article called Getting to the Bottom of Knee Pain in Women.

899
00:39:23.210 --> 00:39:23.290
Oh.

900
00:39:23.670 --> 00:39:23.870
Okay.

901
00:39:24.470 --> 00:39:29.110
Knee pain in women caused by their butts, question mark, the article asks.

902
00:39:29.730 --> 00:39:37.570
It says, if you're experiencing knee pain and you go to a physical therapist, they might ask you, are you using your butt?

903
00:39:38.370 --> 00:39:42.050
If the pain is not from, like, an obvious injury, you know?

904
00:39:42.050 --> 00:39:47.030
Well, this physical therapist says, I always start with the glutes.

905
00:39:47.410 --> 00:39:58.730
I guess a lot of times knee pain can be caused by either tight, weak hips or weak glutes because the glutes are like your stabilizer.

906
00:39:58.730 --> 00:40:03.530
And so they will often want you to increase your glutes.

907
00:40:04.030 --> 00:40:09.090
But the question here is if you're supposed to clench your buttocks or not.

908
00:40:09.270 --> 00:40:10.010
When you walk.

909
00:40:10.010 --> 00:40:21.770
And so while, yes, weak glutes could be the root of your knee problem, I read a different article called To Clench or Not to Clench Your Butt.

910
00:40:21.770 --> 00:40:24.450
That is the question by Brooke Thomas.

911
00:40:24.970 --> 00:40:28.750
She says, do not perma-clench your butt.

912
00:40:29.050 --> 00:40:30.410
Don't perma-clench it.

913
00:40:30.490 --> 00:40:31.550
What's a perma-clench?

914
00:40:31.710 --> 00:40:34.570
That's, I think, where you're just clenching for no reason.

915
00:40:34.930 --> 00:40:36.890
Why would you clench for no reason?

916
00:40:36.990 --> 00:40:38.850
To take the pressure off your knees.

917
00:40:39.530 --> 00:40:42.810
She said it can lead to other probleMs.

918
00:40:43.170 --> 00:40:46.170
It can lead to wear and tear on your lumbar discs.

919
00:40:46.670 --> 00:40:49.470
You can get too tight of a pelvic floor.

920
00:40:50.250 --> 00:40:51.650
I guess that's bad.

921
00:40:52.290 --> 00:40:57.690
Instead of clenching, just do good glute workouts to build up the whole muscle.

922
00:40:57.890 --> 00:40:58.070
Okay?

923
00:40:59.050 --> 00:41:02.610
I know that we have not gotten very far into this episode.

924
00:41:03.150 --> 00:41:04.750
Should we take a break, though?

925
00:41:04.950 --> 00:41:07.130
And then we'll come back and we'll break down the reSt.

926
00:41:07.130 --> 00:41:13.070
Yeah, because when we come back, the Scott family is checking in at the restaurant.

927
00:41:13.550 --> 00:41:14.010
Yes.

928
00:41:23.130 --> 00:41:24.850
Scott family table is ready.

929
00:41:25.330 --> 00:41:26.630
