Michael realizes that Helene is 58.

969
00:42:52.810 --> 00:42:55.970
And you can tell this hits him pretty hard.

970
00:42:55.970 --> 00:42:58.910
We had a fan catch, though, from Allison H.

971
00:42:59.050 --> 00:43:02.290
in Louisville, Kentucky, and many others, by the way,

972
00:43:02.490 --> 00:43:05.590
who said, I think there's a math error.

973
00:43:06.510 --> 00:43:08.190
Helene says she's 49.

974
00:43:08.750 --> 00:43:10.990
Pam says it's the ninth year in a row.

975
00:43:10.990 --> 00:43:19.570
But if she first celebrated her 49th birthday on her 49th birthday, that counts as one of the nine.

976
00:43:19.790 --> 00:43:27.150
So you would actually add 49 plus eight additional birthdays, which means Helene is really turning 57.

977
00:43:28.070 --> 00:43:29.190
Nice catch.

978
00:43:29.610 --> 00:43:30.030
Yeah.

979
00:43:30.410 --> 00:43:38.310
So when I was trading messages with Charlie Grandy about this episode, he said that what he remembers most about working with Seth Gordon

980
00:43:38.310 --> 00:43:47.590
was the fact that me, John, Steve, and Linda were going to be locked at this same table for, like, four big scenes in a row.

981
00:43:47.950 --> 00:43:53.610
And it became this big question, how are we going to visually differentiate these scenes?

982
00:43:53.730 --> 00:43:56.470
How are we going to make them feel alive?

983
00:43:56.470 --> 00:43:56.990
Right.

984
00:43:57.710 --> 00:44:02.850
And Charlie said, if you rewatch it, you can really see what a great job he did.

985
00:44:03.030 --> 00:44:04.870
He added multiple angles.

986
00:44:04.990 --> 00:44:07.610
He keeps flipping sides to keep it interesting.

987
00:44:07.910 --> 00:44:15.690
And by mostly framing out the other tables, he does a great job of shrinking what was a really big space

988
00:44:15.690 --> 00:44:20.650
and, quote, imprisoning you in Michael's awkwardness.

989
00:44:21.130 --> 00:44:22.910
Ooh, that's so artsy.

990
00:44:23.070 --> 00:44:23.690
I know.

991
00:44:23.690 --> 00:44:25.070
And it's really true.

992
00:44:25.070 --> 00:44:35.730
I started rewatching these scenes, and we only used two cameras, but in each of the scenes, they set them up a little differently.

993
00:44:35.730 --> 00:44:38.930
So you didn't feel like you were coming back to the same table.

994
00:44:39.050 --> 00:44:44.730
And as the scenes go on, the camera gets closer and closer and closer.

995
00:44:44.730 --> 00:44:49.470
So you really are, like, going into Michael's, like, little mind.

996
00:44:49.790 --> 00:44:50.690
It's cool.

997
00:44:50.890 --> 00:44:51.790
It's really cool.

998
00:44:52.070 --> 00:45:00.930
Well, we're going to go from this talk of being 49 nine years in a row, but actually being 58 with more sexy talk.

999
00:45:01.430 --> 00:45:03.750
What name should she be called, Nana or Grandma?

1000
00:45:04.310 --> 00:45:04.710
Mm-hmm.

1001
00:45:04.850 --> 00:45:06.590
Michael's really feeling it now.

1002
00:45:06.850 --> 00:45:07.670
He is.

1003
00:45:07.670 --> 00:45:11.670
I noticed something at nine minutes and six seconds in this scene.

1004
00:45:12.010 --> 00:45:12.170
What?

1005
00:45:12.570 --> 00:45:16.550
Do you notice how Steve eats his food as Michael Scott?

1006
00:45:17.190 --> 00:45:20.110
It's exactly how he ate in Dinner Party.

1007
00:45:20.550 --> 00:45:23.390
Well, he kind of scrapes the fork with his teeth.

1008
00:45:23.750 --> 00:45:24.210
Yes.

1009
00:45:24.470 --> 00:45:31.070
He eats tiny amounts of food off the tip of the fork with his very front teeth.

1010
00:45:31.070 --> 00:45:34.010
He doesn't put the fork all the way in his mouth.

1011
00:45:34.430 --> 00:45:37.230
He, like, bites it off the tip of the fork.

1012
00:45:37.730 --> 00:45:38.710
It's very interesting.

1013
00:45:38.790 --> 00:45:40.530
He does not eat this way in real life.

1014
00:45:40.530 --> 00:45:42.370
I've dined with him many times.

1015
00:45:42.750 --> 00:45:46.070
This is clearly a Michael Scott eating choice.

1016
00:45:46.310 --> 00:45:53.370
It's either a Michael Scott eating choice or it's Steve the actor not wanting to eat the prop food and making the best of it.

1017
00:45:53.390 --> 00:45:55.170
Because I would do something similar.

1018
00:45:55.170 --> 00:46:01.510
I would just put the tiniest amount, like, on the end of the fork or spoon so I didn't have to eat too much of it.

1019
00:46:01.750 --> 00:46:14.030
Well, now I guess I'd have to watch Steve's other films and see if he's eating in any of them and see if this is just his actor way of eating or if it was a character choice.

1020
00:46:14.170 --> 00:46:14.730
I'll investigate.

1021
00:46:15.330 --> 00:46:15.770
Investigate.

1022
00:46:15.830 --> 00:46:21.650
Because with prop food, when you start out, it's usually really fresh and warm and they've made it ready for you to eat.

1023
00:46:21.650 --> 00:46:28.810
But as each take goes, it gets colder and colder and a little bit more wilty, depending what you're eating.

1024
00:46:29.050 --> 00:46:32.630
And I just found early on the smaller bites are better.

1025
00:46:33.050 --> 00:46:33.230
True.

1026
00:46:33.870 --> 00:46:36.390
It's also lunchtime back at Dunder Mifflin.

1027
00:46:36.710 --> 00:46:41.890
